  artworks:
  - imageName: 0659 Affandi, Bistro in Paris M
    title: Bistro in Paris
    description: "This work titled Bistro in Paris is an exceptional one. It is world
      famous because it got the second prize at the Biennale in Venice in 1954. Affandi
      was at the time already in Europe. In '53, he painted this, and in '53, he
      was also participating in the Biennale of S\xE3o Paulo, and his works there
      attracted the curator of the Venice Biennale in '54. That's why he was invited
      to participate in the Biennale in '84 in Venice. He sent more than one painting,
      but this got the second prize, which was of course a big achievement. But Affandi
      was not happy. Affandi said, I should have got the first prize. And you know
      who got the first prize? It was the great surrealist Max Ernest. So I think
      second prize is already a very big achievement. But Afandi has a different
      perception. That's also what shows the greatness of Afandi"
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f5af115f49fe5d449a87d5a1137bc681, type: 3}
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4bf5d6ea58120994192be8850f040553, type: 3}
